6
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:25,510
Here is the definition
of arrhythmia. Arrhythmia

7
00:00:25,510 --> 00:00:28,830
is defined as not
normal sinus rhythm.

8
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:33,670
So first you have to know
what's normal sinus rhythm.

9
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:37,870
As we have learned,
normal heartbeat is

10
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:42,030
originated from the
sinus node with a rate in

11
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:45,650
the range of 60 to
100 beats per minute.

12
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:49,710
It should be regular
and follow the

13
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:53,110
normal conduction
sequence as shown here.

14
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:58,590
Any deviation from the normal
sinus rhythm is arrhythmia.

15
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:03,390
Note that some arrhythmia
could be physiological.

16
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,970
For example,

17
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:06,750
if you exercise,

18
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:09,570
you can have sinus tachycardia.

19
00:01:09,730 --> 00:01:13,790
We'll focus on clinically
significant arrhythmia.

20
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:21,290
Here is the arrhythmia
classification and mechanisms.

21
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,290
Depending on the heart rate,

22
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:28,770
Arrhythmia can be classified
as Brady Arrhythmia

23
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:33,770
if the heart rate is less
than 60 beats per minute.

24
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:36,090
The number is for adults.

25
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:39,290
Brady Arrhythmia
is caused by either

26
00:01:39,290 --> 00:01:44,630
conduction block and or
reduced automaticity.

27
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:50,370
If heart rate is more than
100 beats per minute, it's

28
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:54,530
defined as Tachy Arrhythmia.
Tachyallythmia can be

29
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:58,470
caused by one or more of
the following mechanisms

30
00:01:58,470 --> 00:02:04,870
increased automaticity,
triggered activity, and reentry.

31
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:09,050
Reentry is considered
as the most common

32
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:12,030
mechanism for all
tachyallythmians.

33
00:02:13,890 --> 00:02:18,670
For tachyallythmians,
depending on the sites where

34
00:02:18,670 --> 00:02:22,910
the allysmians are
originated, they can be

35
00:02:22,910 --> 00:02:27,270
classified as supraventricular
arrhythmias if they

36
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:32,710
are originated from a site
at his bundle or above.

37
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:36,910
Because supraventricular
arrhythmias are typically

38
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:40,630
associated with normal
ventricular activation,

39
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:45,290
unless there is a pre
-existing abnormality in

40
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:50,070
the ventricles, such as
bundle branch block, They

41
00:02:50,090 --> 00:02:55,790
typically produce normal
narrow QRS complex,

42
00:02:56,070 --> 00:03:00,650
so narrow QRS
tachycardia is the

43
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:04,090
feature of supraventricular
tachycardia.

44
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:08,750
Any alizomere originated
from a site below

45
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:12,850
the his bundle is
defined as ventricular

46
00:03:12,850 --> 00:03:16,550
alizomere. Because in
ventricular arrhythmia,

47
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:20,270
the ventricular activation
will be abnormal,

48
00:03:20,630 --> 00:03:23,650
it will produce an abnormal

49
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:28,370
widened QRS complex. Thus,

50
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:34,130
wide QRS tachycardia is
typically ventricular origin.

51
00:03:36,730 --> 00:03:41,410
Listed here are the basic
arrhythmia mechanisms.

52
00:03:41,590 --> 00:03:44,970
They are divided
into two categories.

53
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:45,850
First,

54
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:49,730
abnormal impulse
initiation. The

55
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:52,990
second is abnormal
impulse conduction.

56
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:57,550
Under abnormal impulse
initiation, they are

57
00:03:57,550 --> 00:04:02,130
abnormal automaticity
and tricked activity.

58
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:05,850
Under abnormal automaticity,

59
00:04:05,890 --> 00:04:09,950
they are altered
normal automaticity and

60
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:14,470
abnormal automaticity.
Under tricked activity,

61
00:04:14,810 --> 00:04:18,390
they are early
after depolarization

62
00:04:18,390 --> 00:04:23,630
and delayed after
depolarization .

63
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:27,810
On the abnormal
impulse conduction,

64
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:31,850
there are conduction
block and reentry.

65
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:36,570
Conduction block can happen
in different sites in

66
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:41,490
the heart, such as at the
sinus node atrial junction,

67
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:46,090
in the AV node, his bundle,
and the bundle branches.

68
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:52,630
Reentry can happen due to
structural or anatomical

69
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:56,450
abnormalities such as
the accessory pathways,

70
00:04:56,550 --> 00:04:57,930
scar tissues,

71
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:00,930
or due to functional changes

72
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:03,970
without structural change.

73
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:07,310
We'll discuss each of these in

74
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:10,090
more detail in the
next few slides.

75
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:17,230
or altered normal
automaticity. The

76
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:20,390
normal heartbeat is
from the sinus node.

77
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:24,590
The altered normal
automaticity refers to

78
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:29,870
either increased or
decreased sinus rates. If

79
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:33,090
the sinus rate is above
100 beats per minute,

80
00:05:33,090 --> 00:05:38,090
it's sinus tachycardia.
Sinus tachycardia is

81
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:41,810
usually secondary and
could be physiological.

82
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:43,770
For example,

83
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:47,790
sinus tachycardia can
be seen during exercise.

84
00:05:48,290 --> 00:05:51,370
Sinus tachycardia can also be

85
00:05:51,370 --> 00:05:55,410
secondary to disease
states like fever,

86
00:05:55,990 --> 00:06:01,010
psilotoxicosis, etc.
There is a clinical

87
00:06:01,010 --> 00:06:05,570
syndrome called inappropriate
sinus tachycardia,

88
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:09,750
seen in patients
without obvious causes.

89
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:13,870
If the sinus rate is
less than 60 beats

90
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:18,150
per minute, it's called
sinus bradycardia.

91
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:21,190
It can be physiological,

92
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:23,390
seen in at rest. Next,

93
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:27,410
pathological sinus
bradycardia is typically

94
00:06:27,410 --> 00:06:32,950
seen in sick sinus
syndrome or 3S syndrome,

95
00:06:33,610 --> 00:06:36,470
a degenerative
disease in cardiac

96
00:06:36,470 --> 00:06:39,050
pacemaker conduction system.

97
00:06:41,030 --> 00:06:47,090
Abnormal automaticity refers
to non-pacemaker cells

98
00:06:47,090 --> 00:06:52,470
like atrium myocytes or
ventricular myocytes In certain

99
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:57,390
disease states, like ischemia,
hypoxia, inflammation,

100
00:06:57,970 --> 00:07:01,490
the injured myocytes
gain automaticity.

101
00:07:02,010 --> 00:07:06,570
Because in disease states,
the injured myocytes

102
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:10,650
cannot maintain normal
resting membrane potential.

103
00:07:10,650 --> 00:07:13,670
potential. The resting
membrane potential

104
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:17,850
could rise, and if the
resting membrane potential

105
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:20,810
cannot drop below
the threshold,

106
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:24,050
the fast sodium channel will be

107
00:07:24,050 --> 00:07:27,970
inactivated, as we have
discussed previously

108
00:07:27,970 --> 00:07:31,130
in the action
potential lecture.

109
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:35,590
These cells could be
activated by the L

110
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:39,450
-type calcium channel.
If this happens,

111
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:44,010
the myocyte behaves like
a slow response cell.

112
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:49,230
Depending on where this
happens, it could cause

113
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:52,790
atrial arrhythmia or
ventricular arrhythmia.

114
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:57,090
Tricked activity,

115
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:02,250
TA, is the oscillation
in member potential.

116
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:05,990
It requires a previous
action potential.

117
00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:10,510
If it happens in later phase 2

118
00:08:10,850 --> 00:08:13,450
or in phase 3,

119
00:08:13,690 --> 00:08:18,950
it's called early after
depolarization, EAD.

120
00:08:19,110 --> 00:08:23,930
If it happens in
phase 4, is termed

121
00:08:23,930 --> 00:08:27,590
delayed after
depolarization, DAD.

122
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:33,950
EAD is typically associated
with action potential

123
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:38,710
prolongation, like in
Long-Cottie syndrome,

124
00:08:38,870 --> 00:08:40,970
hypokalemia, etc.

125
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:46,630
EAD is due to reactivation
of the L-type calcium

126
00:08:46,630 --> 00:08:51,270
channel, because these
channels are time-dependent.

127
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:55,400
As time passes, they
can be reactivated.

128
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:58,310
Since heart rate slowing

129
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:02,270
tends to increase QT interval,

130
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:06,550
the risk of EAD increases if

131
00:09:06,550 --> 00:09:08,930
the heart rate is too slow.

132
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:14,370
DAD is associated
with calcium overload.

133
00:09:14,570 --> 00:09:18,610
In conditions of
digital toxicity,

134
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:22,410
reperfusion-induced
arrhythmia and

135
00:09:22,410 --> 00:09:25,450
catecholaminergic
polymorphic ventricular

136
00:09:25,450 --> 00:09:29,490
tachycardia,
abbreviated as C-PVT.

137
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:32,830
As you have learned already

138
00:09:32,830 --> 00:09:35,150
in action potential lecture,

139
00:09:35,590 --> 00:09:39,530
calcium overload will
trigger sodium-calcium

140
00:09:39,530 --> 00:09:43,230
exchanger. Activation
of sodium-calcium

141
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:48,020
exchanger will bring in
more positive charges

142
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:51,970
and depolarize the
membrane potential.

143
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:56,310
Fast heart rate typically
promotes calcium

144
00:09:56,310 --> 00:10:01,490
overload and thus
increases DAD risk.

145
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:07,250
Abnormal impulse conduction.

146
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:10,330
First is the conduction block.

147
00:10:10,450 --> 00:10:14,090
This is easy to
understand. Conduction

148
00:10:14,090 --> 00:10:17,550
blocks are frequently
seen in these sites.

149
00:10:18,210 --> 00:10:23,030
Sino-H exit block,
AV block, left

150
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:26,030
or right-bound
branch block, etc.

151
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:31,270
Another type of abnormal

152
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:33,970
impulse conduction is re-entry.

153
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:39,170
Since re-entry is considered
to be the most common

154
00:10:39,170 --> 00:10:44,130
mechanism for all
tachyarysmias, this is an

155
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:49,310
important concept you have
to understand. Normally, a

156
00:10:49,310 --> 00:10:53,570
heartbeat generated
inside the sinus node will

157
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:57,990
activate the atria, the
AV node, the His-Pukinji

158
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:03,870
system, and the ventricles
once, and then dies out.

159
00:11:03,990 --> 00:11:08,350
In other words, one
heartbeat excites the whole

160
00:11:08,350 --> 00:11:13,130
heart only once. As
shown in the left figure,

161
00:11:13,490 --> 00:11:18,650
an impulse coming from
top will go down through

162
00:11:18,650 --> 00:11:23,430
both left and right
pathways to reach the

163
00:11:23,430 --> 00:11:28,130
bottom. The excitation
will not return back.

164
00:11:29,950 --> 00:11:34,730
If the same impulse
re-excites the

165
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:38,530
heart more than once,
it's called re-entry

166
00:11:38,530 --> 00:11:41,510
as shown in the
right illustration.

167
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:47,190
In the next slide, I'll explain

168
00:11:47,190 --> 00:11:50,410
how the re-entry
could be formed.

169
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:57,790
To form a reentry,
first, it is necessary

170
00:11:57,790 --> 00:12:01,270
to have inhomogeneous
cardiac tissues,

171
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:05,570
either anatomically
or functionally.

172
00:12:05,890 --> 00:12:09,230
As shown in the left figure,

173
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:13,910
the left and right
pathways have different

174
00:12:13,910 --> 00:12:18,530
conduction velocity
CV, and effective

175
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:23,050
refractory period
ERP. In other words,

176
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:25,990
they have different
electrophysiological

177
00:12:25,990 --> 00:12:31,770
properties, or inhomogeneous.
The left side pathway

178
00:12:31,770 --> 00:12:37,030
has slow conduction
velocity, or slow pathway,

179
00:12:37,250 --> 00:12:42,170
but the slow pathway
has short ERP. The

180
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:46,170
right side pathway has
fast conduction velocity,

181
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:51,270
or fast pathway,
but it has long ERP.

182
00:12:51,910 --> 00:12:55,110
Let's look how excitation will

183
00:12:55,110 --> 00:12:57,410
be conducted in this case.

184
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:01,270
When excitation
comes from the top,

185
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:06,230
it will be conducted by
both the fast and the

186
00:13:06,230 --> 00:13:10,150
slow pathways. Because
the fast pathway

187
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:14,710
conducts faster, it will
reach the bottom first.

188
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:20,550
The excitation conducted
by the fast pathway

189
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:24,930
could even invade into
the distal portion of the

190
00:13:24,930 --> 00:13:29,930
slow pathway in a
retrograde manner. However,

191
00:13:30,290 --> 00:13:34,550
when the two excitation
fronts, the anti

192
00:13:34,550 --> 00:13:37,150
-grade conduction
by the slow pathway

193
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:40,290
and the retrograde
conduction from the

194
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:43,830
fast pathway collide,
the excitation

195
00:13:43,830 --> 00:13:47,530
will stop and no re
-entry would occur.

196
00:13:47,970 --> 00:13:50,550
This is the case with regular

197
00:13:50,550 --> 00:13:54,970
beads A1, A1, A1
beads as shown.

198
00:13:56,080 --> 00:14:00,110
Things will be different
when you have a short

199
00:14:00,110 --> 00:14:04,550
preliminary bead A2, as
shown on the right figure.

200
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:07,590
At preliminary bead A2,

201
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:11,990
because the excitation
arrives so early,

202
00:14:12,270 --> 00:14:16,400
the right side fast
pathway is not recovered

203
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:21,770
due to its long ERP.
Thus, the conduction will

204
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:26,250
be blocked in the fast
pathway, as indicated.

205
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:29,710
Since the left
side slow pathway

206
00:14:29,710 --> 00:14:34,330
has short ERP and
recovers sooner,

207
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:38,550
the premature excitation
A2 can go down

208
00:14:38,550 --> 00:14:41,710
along the slow
pathway to reach the

209
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:44,790
bottom, although
it conducts slower.

210
00:14:45,430 --> 00:14:48,310
the right side fast pathway

211
00:14:48,310 --> 00:14:51,650
could recover as time goes.

212
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:55,770
So when excitation travel down,

213
00:14:56,170 --> 00:14:58,910
slowly through
the left side slow

214
00:14:58,910 --> 00:15:02,470
pathway to reach
the bottom. And when

215
00:15:02,470 --> 00:15:05,230
the right side fast
pathway recovers,

216
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:10,030
the excitation could
activate the fast pathway

217
00:15:10,030 --> 00:15:14,450
retrograded from the
bottom. And when the

218
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:19,270
excitation reaches the
previously blocked area, and

219
00:15:19,270 --> 00:15:23,450
if the area is already
recovered, then the

220
00:15:23,450 --> 00:15:28,770
excitation could continue.
This forms a re-entry.

221
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:33,610
In other words, the
same excitation returns

222
00:15:33,610 --> 00:15:37,630
back and re-excites
the tissue again.

223
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:43,910
Now you should
know these are the

224
00:15:43,910 --> 00:15:47,490
requirements to form re-entry.

225
00:15:47,810 --> 00:15:52,590
First, there should be
a unidirectional block.

226
00:15:52,670 --> 00:15:56,070
As shown, the excitation
cannot propagate

227
00:15:56,070 --> 00:16:00,490
from up-down, but it allows to

228
00:16:00,490 --> 00:16:04,560
propagate in a reversed
direction. Second,

229
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:09,090
there is a slow conduction,
which affords time

230
00:16:09,090 --> 00:16:13,130
for the previously
refractory tissue to recover.

231
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:14,570
Third,

232
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:17,390
there is a recovery
of previously

233
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:20,310
excited proximal tissue.

234
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:23,130
When all these requirements

235
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:27,010
are met, then reentry can form.

236
00:16:28,710 --> 00:16:33,150
Here is the concept
of wavelength.

237
00:16:34,110 --> 00:16:36,990
When re-entry happens,

238
00:16:37,750 --> 00:16:41,510
in the re-entry circuit
there are two parts.

239
00:16:41,950 --> 00:16:45,110
First is the tissue has been

240
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:48,090
excited and in refractory.

241
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:54,550
It's called wavelength. The
second part is tissue out

242
00:16:54,550 --> 00:17:00,590
of refractory can be excited,
called excitable gap.

243
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:05,090
Wavelength is determined
by two factors,

244
00:17:05,330 --> 00:17:09,950
the effective refractory
period ERP and

245
00:17:09,950 --> 00:17:15,310
conduction velocity CV.
It can be calculated by

246
00:17:15,310 --> 00:17:21,710
this equation, Wavelength
equals CV times ERP.

247
00:17:22,030 --> 00:17:26,220
Since the re-entry
circuit equals

248
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:30,690
Wavelength plus Excitable Gap,

249
00:17:31,450 --> 00:17:36,090
the Wavelength needs to
be less than the re-entry

250
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:41,470
circuit in order to sustain
re-entry. When wavelength

251
00:17:41,470 --> 00:17:46,710
reaches the total length of
the circuit, then anything

252
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:52,330
will be in refractory and
reentry would be terminated.

253
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:54,930
From here, you should know

254
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:58,010
that by increasing wavelength,

255
00:17:58,210 --> 00:18:03,430
it will decrease
reentry risk. On the

256
00:18:03,430 --> 00:18:06,790
other hand, if you
shorten wavelengths,

257
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:10,370
then reentry risk increases.

258
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:14,490
This is why many antiarrhythmic

259
00:18:14,490 --> 00:18:19,490
medications work to
increase ERP to increase

260
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:23,290
wavelengths and
decrease reentry.

261
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:29,270
If you still have
difficulty in understanding

262
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:32,380
the relationship
between wavelengths

263
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:36,650
and re-entry circuit,
I would like to give

264
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:40,830
you this analogy. Look
at this toy train.

265
00:18:41,210 --> 00:18:44,450
You can envision
the length of the

266
00:18:44,450 --> 00:18:49,710
train as the wavelength
and the length

267
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:53,650
of the track as the
re-entry circuit.

268
00:18:53,770 --> 00:18:58,270
In order to run the train,
the length of the train

269
00:18:58,270 --> 00:19:01,790
needs to be shorter than
the length of the track.

270
00:19:01,910 --> 00:19:07,250
Otherwise, you cannot play.
On the other hand, if the

271
00:19:07,250 --> 00:19:11,490
length of the train is very
short, then it's possible

272
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:15,390
that you can fit more than
one train on the track.

273
00:19:15,730 --> 00:19:19,990
Hope this helps in
understanding the concept.

274
00:19:22,810 --> 00:19:28,270
Since there is always an
excitable gap in reentry

275
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:33,810
circuit, if you can excite
the tissue in excitable

276
00:19:33,810 --> 00:19:39,150
gap by artificial pacing
or electrical shock,

277
00:19:39,230 --> 00:19:43,810
then you can stop the
reentry. This is one of

278
00:19:43,810 --> 00:19:47,450
the important
electrophysiological features of

279
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:52,430
reentry allusion. It can
be terminated by pacing.

280
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:56,570
It's called anti
-tachycardia pacing.

281
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:03,530
Here are some of the
potential reentry circuits.

282
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:07,410
Panel A shows the model of

283
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:10,810
wavelengths and excitable gap.

284
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:14,270
B shows the Wolff-Parkinson

285
00:20:14,270 --> 00:20:18,070
-White syndrome or WPW syndrome.

286
00:20:18,190 --> 00:20:23,570
In WPW syndrome, there
is an accessory pathway

287
00:20:23,570 --> 00:20:28,110
in addition to the normal
AV node hiss-bounded

288
00:20:28,110 --> 00:20:32,830
pathway, linking the
atria and the ventricles.

289
00:20:32,830 --> 00:20:38,250
The re-entry involves
both atria and ventricles,

290
00:20:38,310 --> 00:20:43,130
the whole heart, so
it's a micro re-entry.

291
00:20:43,550 --> 00:20:47,130
It's also an
anatomical re-entry

292
00:20:47,130 --> 00:20:50,570
because there is an
accessory pathways.

293
00:20:52,110 --> 00:20:55,530
Penelty shows re-entry
could happen at the

294
00:20:55,530 --> 00:21:00,390
tiny junction of Purkinje
fibers and myocytes.

295
00:21:00,950 --> 00:21:03,070
This shows the re-entry could

296
00:21:03,070 --> 00:21:05,910
happen within the
muscle bundles.

297
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:10,270
These are micro re
-entries and could be

298
00:21:10,270 --> 00:21:14,270
functional re-entries
without abnormal structure.

299
00:21:14,470 --> 00:21:18,070
So re-entry can
happen in different

300
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:20,410
parts of the cardiac tissue.

301
00:21:20,550 --> 00:21:22,830
Some may have very large

302
00:21:22,830 --> 00:21:26,050
circuit like in WPW syndrome,

303
00:21:26,130 --> 00:21:32,910
while some may have very
tiny circuit like in

304
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:36,610
atrioventricular node
re-entrant tachycardia.

305
00:21:39,270 --> 00:21:44,050
Now we'll look at common
clinical allysmias.

306
00:21:44,290 --> 00:21:48,650
First, we'll look
at blade allysmias.

307
00:21:48,770 --> 00:21:53,410
The potential mechanisms
for blade allysmias are

308
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:59,330
failure of impulse generation
or decreased automaticity.

309
00:21:59,330 --> 00:22:04,450
This includes sinus
bradycardia or sinus arrest,

310
00:22:04,450 --> 00:22:08,230
typically seen in sick
sinus syndrome. mechanism.

311
00:22:08,570 --> 00:22:11,970
The other mechanism
is failure of

312
00:22:11,970 --> 00:22:15,430
impulse propagation,
or conduction block.

313
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:18,390
The common conduction
block sites

314
00:22:18,390 --> 00:22:23,130
include sinoatrial
block, AV block, etc.

315
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:28,800
Now we'll look
at tachylysmians.

316
00:22:29,770 --> 00:22:32,990
Tachylysmians are
caused by one or

317
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:36,430
more of these three
basic mechanisms,

318
00:22:36,550 --> 00:22:40,130
abnormal automaticity,
trickle activity,

319
00:22:40,130 --> 00:22:44,250
or re-entry. As
already discussed,

320
00:22:44,710 --> 00:22:48,670
tachylysmians are divided
into supraventricular

321
00:22:48,670 --> 00:22:52,530
tachylysmians and
ventricular alesimians.

322
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:55,670
Supraventricular
tachylysmians are

323
00:22:55,670 --> 00:23:01,030
originated at the his
bundle or above. Because

324
00:23:01,030 --> 00:23:03,770
the ventricles are
excited normally,

325
00:23:03,930 --> 00:23:10,230
thus the QRS is typically
narrow with the exception

326
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:13,930
of pre-existing
ventricular abnormalities.

327
00:23:14,730 --> 00:23:18,290
While the ventricular
tachylythmias are

328
00:23:18,290 --> 00:23:23,350
originated below the his
bundle and are associated

329
00:23:23,350 --> 00:23:26,230
with abnormal
ventricular activation,

330
00:23:26,290 --> 00:23:32,410
the QRS complex will
be abnormal, widened.

331
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:38,630
This table lists
various supraventricular

332
00:23:38,630 --> 00:23:41,750
tachyralesmias and
their mechanisms.

333
00:23:42,510 --> 00:23:45,650
We will discuss some
of the important

334
00:23:45,650 --> 00:23:49,670
supraventricular alesmias
in the next few slides.

335
00:23:52,090 --> 00:23:55,550
First, we'll look
at atrial flutter.

336
00:23:55,870 --> 00:23:58,790
It's known that
atrial flutter is

337
00:23:58,790 --> 00:24:02,770
caused by a reentry
in the right atrium.

338
00:24:02,970 --> 00:24:07,230
The reentry involves a
narrow region between

339
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:10,970
inferior vena cava and
the tricuspid valve.

340
00:24:10,970 --> 00:24:15,750
This is known as the
cavil tricuspid isthmus.

341
00:24:15,890 --> 00:24:20,010
As a result, casted
ablation of this

342
00:24:20,010 --> 00:24:24,770
isthmus could be used
to cure this allysmia.

343
00:24:26,810 --> 00:24:30,130
Next is atrial fibrillation.

344
00:24:30,390 --> 00:24:34,430
Atrial fibrillation is
the most common clinically

345
00:24:34,430 --> 00:24:38,470
significant allysmia.
Atrial fibrillation

346
00:24:38,470 --> 00:24:42,710
is caused by multiple re
-entries in both atria.

347
00:24:43,210 --> 00:24:47,510
Atrial fibrillation requires
a trigger or ectopic

348
00:24:47,510 --> 00:24:54,010
fossa to initiate the
alethymia, and a substrate, the

349
00:24:54,010 --> 00:24:59,130
remodeled atria, with
dilatation, fibrosis, to

350
00:24:59,130 --> 00:25:03,590
support multiple re-entries
to maintain the alethymia.

351
00:25:03,590 --> 00:25:08,970
In other words, in normal,
healthy subjects, it's

352
00:25:08,970 --> 00:25:12,650
not easy to induce and
maintain atrial fibrillation.

353
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:15,870
Since most triggers are coming

354
00:25:15,870 --> 00:25:17,870
from the pulmonary vein,

355
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:22,850
this is why pulmonary
vein isolation is used

356
00:25:22,850 --> 00:25:26,150
to cure atrial
fibrillation in patients.

357
00:25:28,850 --> 00:25:32,510
We'll look at
atrioventricular nodal

358
00:25:32,510 --> 00:25:38,210
reentrant tachycardia,
AVNRT. By the name,

359
00:25:38,210 --> 00:25:41,390
you should know the
mechanism is reentry.

360
00:25:41,730 --> 00:25:44,710
In AVNRT patients,

361
00:25:44,930 --> 00:25:49,270
the AV node region is
allegedly dissociated

362
00:25:49,270 --> 00:25:54,250
into a fast pathway
and a slow pathway, so

363
00:25:54,250 --> 00:25:58,380
-called AV node dual
pathway electrophysiology.

364
00:25:58,570 --> 00:26:01,410
As we have discussed already,

365
00:26:01,830 --> 00:26:04,790
a preliminary beat
is necessary to

366
00:26:04,790 --> 00:26:09,490
initiate AVNRT as
shown in the figure.

367
00:26:10,770 --> 00:26:15,970
Currently, cast ablation
of the slow pathway is

368
00:26:15,970 --> 00:26:19,970
used to cure this alizmia
because because fast

369
00:26:19,970 --> 00:26:24,790
pathway ablation has higher
risk to induce AV block.

370
00:26:26,690 --> 00:26:31,530
Now we'll look at
atrioventricular

371
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:35,010
reentrant tachycardia, AVRT.

372
00:26:35,280 --> 00:26:39,530
The arrhythmia is caused
by an accessory pathway,

373
00:26:39,530 --> 00:26:44,430
or in some patients,
multiple accessory pathways

374
00:26:44,430 --> 00:26:48,170
connecting the atrio
and the ventricles.

375
00:26:48,810 --> 00:26:55,350
In Wolff-Pakinsen
-White WPW syndrome or

376
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:58,730
pre-excitation
syndrome, the accessory

377
00:26:58,730 --> 00:27:03,110
pathway activation
can be seen on EKG.

378
00:27:03,270 --> 00:27:07,510
However, in some patients,
the accessory pathways

379
00:27:07,510 --> 00:27:12,910
could be concealed, meaning
the EKG could be normal.

380
00:27:13,620 --> 00:27:16,310
Ablation of the
accessor pathway

381
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:19,310
is used to cure the arrhythmia.

382
00:27:19,490 --> 00:27:26,210
In AVRT, depending on the
reentry circuit, if the

383
00:27:26,210 --> 00:27:31,230
ventricles are activated
normally by the Purkinje system,

384
00:27:31,230 --> 00:27:36,250
then the QRS complex
is normal or narrow.

385
00:27:36,260 --> 00:27:41,710
If the range circuit
is reversed, ventricles

386
00:27:41,710 --> 00:27:46,110
are activated by the
accessory pathway, then

387
00:27:46,110 --> 00:27:50,850
the class complex is
abnormal or widened.

388
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:58,190
As a minimum, you'll have
to know WPW syndrome,

389
00:27:58,230 --> 00:28:03,930
and you'll learn this in
EKG lecture, the changes,

390
00:28:04,070 --> 00:28:07,190
the delta wave,
short PR interval,

391
00:28:07,410 --> 00:28:09,930
and wide QIS complex.

392
00:28:13,610 --> 00:28:16,730
Now we'll look at the
ventricular arrhythmia.

393
00:28:19,130 --> 00:28:22,690
Ventricular arrhythmias
are always with

394
00:28:22,690 --> 00:28:27,630
abnormal widened
QRS complex because

395
00:28:27,630 --> 00:28:30,950
the ventricles are
activated abnormally.

396
00:28:31,270 --> 00:28:34,050
We will look at premature

397
00:28:34,050 --> 00:28:36,250
ventricular contraction PVC,

398
00:28:36,450 --> 00:28:39,890
ventricular tachycardia and

399
00:28:39,890 --> 00:28:42,230
ventricular fibrillation .

400
00:28:44,890 --> 00:28:49,230
Premature ventricular
contraction can be caused

401
00:28:49,230 --> 00:28:53,970
by any of these mechanisms,
abnormal automaticity,

402
00:28:54,220 --> 00:28:58,050
triggered activity, or
re-entry, as shown here.

403
00:28:59,270 --> 00:29:04,910
PVC results in wide
QIS complex on EKG.

404
00:29:06,860 --> 00:29:11,630
Next, we'll look at
ventricular tachycardia, VT.

405
00:29:11,830 --> 00:29:18,350
VT is typically divided
into monomorphic VT and

406
00:29:18,350 --> 00:29:22,650
polymorphic VT, depending
on the shape of the

407
00:29:22,650 --> 00:29:29,090
QRS complex. If the QRS
complex is more or less

408
00:29:29,090 --> 00:29:33,470
the same, it's monomorphic
ventricular tachycardia.

409
00:29:33,470 --> 00:29:37,910
If the QIS complex keeps
changing its shape,

410
00:29:37,910 --> 00:29:41,750
it's the polymorphic
ventricular tachycardia.

411
00:29:42,270 --> 00:29:44,990
Monomorphic
ventricular tachycardia

412
00:29:44,990 --> 00:29:47,950
is typically seen
in patients with

413
00:29:47,950 --> 00:29:51,930
structural heart
disease like ischemia,

414
00:29:52,890 --> 00:29:56,970
non-ischemic
cardiomyopsy, alysmogenic

415
00:29:56,970 --> 00:30:00,750
right ventricular
dysplasia. The mechanism

416
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:05,810
is predominantly
reentry. However,

417
00:30:06,310 --> 00:30:10,230
some monomorphic VT
could also happen

418
00:30:10,230 --> 00:30:13,230
in structurally
normal hearts called

419
00:30:13,230 --> 00:30:16,070
idiopathic ventricular
tachycardia.

420
00:30:16,210 --> 00:30:21,130
One type is outflow tract
ventricular tachycardia.

421
00:30:21,270 --> 00:30:25,410
It's believed to be caused
by tricked activity.

422
00:30:25,590 --> 00:30:29,210
Another type is
fascicular ventricular

423
00:30:29,210 --> 00:30:32,870
tachycardia. It's
caused by reentry.

424
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:41,050
Polymorphic VT. In polymorphic
VT, the QRS complex

425
00:30:41,050 --> 00:30:47,010
keeps changing. A specific type
of polymorphic VT is termed

426
00:30:47,010 --> 00:30:51,210
to solder the points,
meaning twisting the points.

427
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:55,850
Polymorphic VT is
typically associated with

428
00:30:55,850 --> 00:31:00,610
lung Coty syndrome, or
cardiac channel process,

429
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:02,810
like Blugger syndrome,

430
00:31:03,250 --> 00:31:07,530
short Coty syndrome,
and catecholaminergic

431
00:31:07,530 --> 00:31:11,430
polymorphic ventricular
tachycardia, CPVT.

432
00:31:14,130 --> 00:31:20,270
Long-COTY syndrome include
inherited or congenital

433
00:31:20,270 --> 00:31:25,550
Long-COTY syndrome and
acquired Long-COTY syndrome.

434
00:31:25,710 --> 00:31:28,330
First, we'll look at the

435
00:31:28,330 --> 00:31:31,450
congenital Long-COTY syndrome.

436
00:31:31,510 --> 00:31:36,550
Many genetic mutations
have been identified in

437
00:31:36,550 --> 00:31:41,530
congenital Long-COTY
syndrome. A majority, three

438
00:31:41,530 --> 00:31:45,250
-quarter, is caused by
the first three types of

439
00:31:45,250 --> 00:31:50,150
mutations, due to defects
in either potassium

440
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:54,210
channel or gain of function
of the sodium channel.

441
00:31:54,350 --> 00:31:58,990
The mechanisms for Long
-Coti syndrome induced

442
00:31:58,990 --> 00:32:02,510
ventricular arrhythmia
is triggered activity,

443
00:32:02,710 --> 00:32:07,790
EAD, as we have discussed.
In these patients,

444
00:32:07,950 --> 00:32:12,550
because sympathetic excitation
can exacerbate channel

445
00:32:12,550 --> 00:32:17,490
abnormalities and further
prolong COT interval,

446
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:19,930
so beta blocker is typically

447
00:32:19,930 --> 00:32:22,990
used to prevent the arrhythmia.

448
00:32:25,190 --> 00:32:28,910
As a minimum, you
are required to know

449
00:32:28,910 --> 00:32:32,770
the congenital Long
-Cottie syndrome.

450
00:32:32,770 --> 00:32:35,890
Note that in some patients, the

451
00:32:35,890 --> 00:32:38,470
channel defect is
poorly cardiac.

452
00:32:38,910 --> 00:32:41,710
They have Long-Cottie syndrome,

453
00:32:41,710 --> 00:32:43,930
but without other problems.

454
00:32:44,090 --> 00:32:45,030
However,

455
00:32:45,350 --> 00:32:48,830
in some patients, the
channel defect could also

456
00:32:48,830 --> 00:32:53,570
affect sensory neuron
leading to hearing loss.

457
00:32:53,570 --> 00:32:57,250
This is why when you
interview the patients,

458
00:32:57,250 --> 00:33:01,290
you have to ask whether
the patients have

459
00:33:01,290 --> 00:33:05,390
a hearing problem in
Lung-COTI patients.

460
00:33:09,590 --> 00:33:15,710
Acquired Lung-COTI syndrome
refers to some people,

461
00:33:15,710 --> 00:33:20,210
normally they have normal
COT interval. However,

462
00:33:20,210 --> 00:33:24,470
when these people take
some medications or under

463
00:33:24,470 --> 00:33:28,590
certain conditions, they
can develop lung COT.

464
00:33:28,690 --> 00:33:33,870
These people may have some
subtle genetic defects.

465
00:33:37,910 --> 00:33:42,390
This table lists some of
the common medications

466
00:33:42,390 --> 00:33:47,310
or conditions which
may lead to Lung-CoT.

467
00:33:47,530 --> 00:33:53,890
Note that here the
class 1C anti-arythmic

468
00:33:53,890 --> 00:33:58,730
medication causes Lung
-CoT, not class 1B.

469
00:34:01,970 --> 00:34:05,990
Here is the minimum
requirement for acquired

470
00:34:05,990 --> 00:34:11,610
short QT syndrome,
especially these A, B,

471
00:34:11,810 --> 00:34:16,030
C, D, E medications,
you have to know.

472
00:34:19,240 --> 00:34:22,150
We'll look at
short QT syndrome.

473
00:34:22,320 --> 00:34:27,410
This is opposite to
long QT due to gain of

474
00:34:27,410 --> 00:34:30,990
function of potassium
channels, leading to

475
00:34:30,990 --> 00:34:36,230
rapid repolarization.
In short QT patients,

476
00:34:36,870 --> 00:34:40,890
the ventricules
repolarize faster with

477
00:34:40,890 --> 00:34:46,010
very short AP duration
and QT interval.

478
00:34:46,090 --> 00:34:49,350
The short action
potential duration results

479
00:34:49,350 --> 00:34:53,810
in short ERP and
short wave lengths,

480
00:34:53,810 --> 00:34:58,150
thus favoring formation
of multiple ranges.

481
00:35:01,560 --> 00:35:05,850
Now we will look at the
Bluger syndrome. This is

482
00:35:05,850 --> 00:35:10,830
due to diminished inward
sodium current, particularly

483
00:35:10,830 --> 00:35:16,210
in right ventricular
outflow tract apicardium

484
00:35:17,470 --> 00:35:23,770
region, leading to apicardial
dispersion of repolarization,

485
00:35:23,770 --> 00:35:27,170
as shown in these
action potential traces.

486
00:35:28,250 --> 00:35:33,350
In EKG, many patients
have characteristic EKG

487
00:35:33,350 --> 00:35:38,490
abnormalities, as shown
here, a curve-type ST

488
00:35:38,490 --> 00:35:43,690
segment elevation in
precordial leads V1 through

489
00:35:43,690 --> 00:35:49,210
V3, which corresponds
to the RV or T region.

490
00:35:51,960 --> 00:35:54,250
You are required to know

491
00:35:54,250 --> 00:35:56,770
Blugard syndrome.
As shown here,

492
00:35:57,130 --> 00:35:59,950
Blugard syndrome
patients have increased

493
00:35:59,950 --> 00:36:02,130
risk to develop ventricular

494
00:36:02,130 --> 00:36:05,050
tachylythmias and
sudden cardiac death.

495
00:36:05,530 --> 00:36:06,890
Typically,

496
00:36:07,130 --> 00:36:12,290
implantable cardioverter
defibrillator is needed

497
00:36:12,290 --> 00:36:16,490
to prevent sudden cardiac
death in these patients.

498
00:36:18,510 --> 00:36:21,990
Now we'll look at
catecholaminergic

499
00:36:21,990 --> 00:36:25,950
polymorphic VT, CPVT.

500
00:36:25,950 --> 00:36:30,350
This is due to genetic
disorders of calcium

501
00:36:30,350 --> 00:36:34,070
release channels or
cardiac low-ending

502
00:36:34,070 --> 00:36:38,590
receptor or their
controlling proteins.

503
00:36:39,110 --> 00:36:42,870
In normal case,
low-ending receptor

504
00:36:42,870 --> 00:36:46,290
should be closed
properly in diastole.

505
00:36:46,410 --> 00:36:49,150
In CPVT patients,

506
00:36:49,510 --> 00:36:52,270
the winding receptor is leaky,

507
00:36:52,490 --> 00:36:55,470
like the leaky faucet here.

508
00:36:55,970 --> 00:37:01,470
The leaky winding receptor
leads to elevated calcium

509
00:37:01,470 --> 00:37:07,310
in diastole, thus activating
the sodium calcium

510
00:37:07,310 --> 00:37:12,270
exchanger and leading to
DAD triggered activity.

511
00:37:13,340 --> 00:37:17,430
CPVT is typically seen
in structurally normal

512
00:37:17,430 --> 00:37:22,810
heart because sympathetic
excitation like exercise

513
00:37:22,810 --> 00:37:28,650
or acute emotion can trick
CPVT. Beta blocker is

514
00:37:28,650 --> 00:37:32,850
typically used to prevent
CPVT in these patients.

515
00:37:35,050 --> 00:37:38,770
Finally, we'll look at
ventricular fibrillation

516
00:37:38,770 --> 00:37:43,630
. Like in atrial
fibrillation, ventricular

517
00:37:43,630 --> 00:37:47,290
fibrillation can be triggered
by any of these three

518
00:37:47,290 --> 00:37:51,770
mechanisms and maintained
by the multiple re

519
00:37:51,770 --> 00:37:56,210
-entries. When ventricular
fibrillation occurs,

520
00:37:56,750 --> 00:38:00,810
the ventricles lose
coordinated contraction and

521
00:38:00,810 --> 00:38:05,510
fail to pump blood, thus
the patient is dying.

522
00:38:06,380 --> 00:38:08,630
Defibrillation is
the only effective

523
00:38:08,630 --> 00:38:11,810
therapy to terminate
atrial fibrillation.

524
00:38:12,370 --> 00:38:15,730
Here is the
question, what's the

525
00:38:15,730 --> 00:38:18,790
mechanism for
defibrillation to work?

526
00:38:22,850 --> 00:38:26,130
Because in ventricular
fibrillation,

527
00:38:26,130 --> 00:38:28,610
there are multiple re-entries.

528
00:38:28,770 --> 00:38:33,190
The electrical shock
can excite all excitable

529
00:38:33,190 --> 00:38:36,730
gaps in multiple re
-entries. Thus, the

530
00:38:36,730 --> 00:38:40,990
whole heart will be in
refractory and wait for

531
00:38:40,990 --> 00:38:45,250
the sinus node to
initiate a new heartbeat.

532
00:38:45,250 --> 00:38:46,790
That's the mechanism.

533
00:38:50,050 --> 00:38:52,990
There are two terminologies,

534
00:38:53,110 --> 00:38:56,990
cardioversion versus
defibrillation.

535
00:38:57,190 --> 00:39:00,910
You have to know that
defibrillation is

536
00:39:00,910 --> 00:39:04,270
used for ventricular
fibrillation only.

537
00:39:04,770 --> 00:39:06,350
In this case,

538
00:39:06,610 --> 00:39:10,950
the synchronizer button
should be turned off,

539
00:39:10,950 --> 00:39:14,570
so the defibrillator
can deliver the shock

540
00:39:14,570 --> 00:39:18,550
immediately once you place
the discharge button.

541
00:39:18,930 --> 00:39:22,890
Because in ventricular
fibrillation,

542
00:39:22,890 --> 00:39:27,830
the EKG signal may
not be large enough

543
00:39:27,830 --> 00:39:30,850
to trigger the shock.
In other words,

544
00:39:31,190 --> 00:39:35,440
the machine may not deliver
the shock if the synchronizer

545
00:39:35,630 --> 00:39:40,950
is on during ventricular
fibrillation. Ventricular

546
00:39:40,950 --> 00:39:44,950
fibrillation normally requires
higher energy compared

547
00:39:44,950 --> 00:39:50,690
with cardioversion, while
cardioversion is used for

548
00:39:50,690 --> 00:39:54,690
other tachyarrhythmias,
such as atrial fibrillation,

549
00:39:55,330 --> 00:39:58,570
proxysmal superventricular
tachycardia, or even

550
00:39:58,570 --> 00:40:02,770
ventricular tachycardia,
but not for ventricular

551
00:40:02,770 --> 00:40:07,400
fibrillation. In this
case, the synchronizer

552
00:40:07,400 --> 00:40:12,410
button should be turned
on and make sure it's

553
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:18,510
synchronized with the R
wave of the QRS complex.

554
00:40:19,030 --> 00:40:23,510
Avoid not on the T
wave. That's important.

555
00:40:24,650 --> 00:40:30,170
So, here is the another
question in cardioversion.

556
00:40:30,330 --> 00:40:33,430
Why the shock should
be synchronized

557
00:40:33,430 --> 00:40:37,870
with the R wave,
not the T wave?

558
00:40:40,610 --> 00:40:45,050
As you know, the QRS complex is

559
00:40:45,050 --> 00:40:48,270
produced by ventricular
depolarization.

560
00:40:48,310 --> 00:40:52,230
The R wave indicates
that the ventricles

561
00:40:52,230 --> 00:40:57,410
are depolarized and
in refractory is

562
00:40:57,410 --> 00:41:00,430
the safest time to
deliver the shock.

563
00:41:01,580 --> 00:41:06,210
If the shock is
delivered on T wave, then

564
00:41:06,210 --> 00:41:09,870
ventricular fibrillation
could be induced because

565
00:41:09,870 --> 00:41:13,810
from the peak of the T
wave to the end of the

566
00:41:13,810 --> 00:41:18,430
T wave, the heart is
in a vulnerable period.

567
00:41:18,630 --> 00:41:21,230
That's why you have to avoid

568
00:41:21,230 --> 00:41:23,890
this period to
deliver the shock.

